IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap3-logic`

-- SECTION 2024, VIOLATIONS AND ENFORCEMENT (7 U.S.C. 2024), lines 1884-1909 of usc07-ch51.txt.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. A function answers MAYBE (BOOLEAN, NUMBER ...) with: JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no
-- in its own words; NOTHING = the text does not say. Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a term of imprisonment is a NUMBER of years (six months is 0.5).
-- This section is a criminal and forfeiture provision: "guilty", "convicted" and "a court" are the text's words; the module decides what the text says follows, never whether someone is guilty.
-- Source is a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.

DECLARE `s 2024 grade of offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 2024 a felony`
    `s 2024 a misdemeanor`

-- WHAT THE TEXT SAYS MAY OR MUST BE IMPOSED for one conviction. Fields:
--   the grade; the most the fine may be (dollars); the least and the most term of imprisonment (years, the least being 0 where the text sets none);
--   whether imprisonment must be imposed (the text's "shall be imprisoned", used for a second or subsequent conviction).
-- A fine is also always allowed alongside imprisonment: the text says "or both", or "and may also be fined".
DECLARE `s 2024 punishment` HAS
    `s 2024 the grade of the offence`                          IS A `s 2024 grade of offence`
    `s 2024 the most the fine may be, in dollars`              IS A NUMBER
    `s 2024 the least term of imprisonment, in years`          IS A NUMBER
    `s 2024 the most term of imprisonment, in years`           IS A NUMBER
    `s 2024 imprisonment must be imposed`                      IS A BOOLEAN

-- HOW THE PROCEEDS OF A CRIMINAL FORFEITURE ARE APPLIED, in the order s 2024(f)(4) gives.
DECLARE `s 2024(f)(4) application of proceeds` HAS
    `s 2024(f)(4)(A) to reimburse the Department of Justice`                  IS A NUMBER
    `s 2024(f)(4)(B) to reimburse the Department of Agriculture Office of Inspector General` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2024(f)(4)(C) to reimburse any Federal or State law enforcement agency` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2024(f)(4)(D) to the Secretary for retail store and wholesale food concern investigations` IS A NUMBER

§ `s 2024 -- violations and enforcement`

§§ `s 2024(a) in general`

-- src:1885 | (a) In general
-- src:1886 | Notwithstanding any other provision of this chapter, the Secretary may provide for the issuance or presentment for redemption of benefits to such person or persons, and at such times and in such manner, as the Secretary deems necessary or appropriate to protect the interests of the United States or to ensure enforcement of the provisions of this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter.
@ref s 2024(a) the Secretary may provide for the issuance or presentment for redemption of benefits as the Secretary deems necessary (src:1885-1886)
-- In plain words: despite anything else in the chapter, the Secretary may decide to whom, when and how benefits are issued or presented for redemption, if the Secretary deems it necessary or appropriate to protect the interests of the United States or to ensure enforcement.
-- Whether the Secretary "deems" it so is the Secretary's judgment: an input.
GIVEN `the Secretary deems the provision necessary or appropriate to protect the interests of the United States or to ensure enforcement of the provisions of this chapter or the regulations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2024(a) the Secretary may provide for the issuance or presentment for redemption of benefits to such person or persons, at such times and in such manner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Secretary deems the provision necessary or appropriate to protect the interests of the United States or to ensure enforcement of the provisions of this chapter or the regulations`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as the Secretary deems necessary or appropriate"
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2024(b) unauthorized use, transfer, acquisition, alteration, or possession of benefits`

-- src:1888 | (1) Subject to the provisions of paragraph (2) of this subsection, whoever knowingly uses, transfers, acquires, alters, or possesses benefits in any manner contrary to this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter
@ref s 2024(b)(1) whoever knowingly uses, transfers, acquires, alters, or possesses benefits contrary to the chapter (src:1888)
-- In plain words: a person who knowingly uses, transfers, acquires, alters or possesses benefits in a way the chapter or its regulations forbid commits the offence whose punishment follows.
GIVEN `the person acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was using, transferring, acquiring, altering, or possessing benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was in a manner contrary to this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2024(b)(1) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person acted knowingly` AND `the act was using, transferring, acquiring, altering, or possessing benefits` AND `the act was in a manner contrary to this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whoever knowingly uses, transfers, acquires, alters, or possesses benefits in any manner contrary to this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter"
            NOTHING

-- src:1888 | shall, if such benefits are of a value of $5,000 or more, be guilty of a felony and shall be fined not more than $250,000 or imprisoned for not more than twenty years, or both, and shall, if such benefits are of a value of $100 or more, but less than $5,000, or if the item used, transferred, acquired, altered, or possessed is a benefit that has a value of $100 or more, but less than $5,000, be guilty of a felony and shall, upon the first conviction thereof, be fined not more than $10,000 or imprisoned for not more than five years, or both, and, upon the second and any subsequent conviction thereof, shall be imprisoned for not less than six months nor more than five years and may also be fined not more than $10,000 or, if such benefits are of a value of less than $100, or if the item used, transferred, acquired, altered, or processed [Footnote: 1 So in original. Probably should be “possessed”.] is a benefit that has a value of less than $100, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and, upon the first conviction thereof, shall be fined not more than $1,000 or imprisoned for not more than one year, or both, and upon the second and any subsequent conviction thereof, shall be imprisoned for not more than one year and may also be fined not more than $1,000.
@ref s 2024(b)(1) the punishment, by the value of the benefits and the number of convictions (src:1888)
-- In plain words: $5,000 or more is a felony (fine up to $250,000 or up to 20 years, or both). $100 or more but under $5,000 is a felony: the first conviction, a fine up to $10,000 or up to 5 years, or both;
-- the second and later, prison of 6 months to 5 years and perhaps also a fine up to $10,000. Under $100 is a misdemeanor: the first conviction, a fine up to $1,000 or up to 1 year, or both;
-- the second and later, prison up to 1 year and perhaps also a fine up to $1,000. The text sets one punishment for $5,000 or more whatever the number of convictions.
-- THE LEAST TERM IS 0 for a first conviction and for $5,000 or more: the text offers "fined ... or imprisoned ..., or both", so a fine alone satisfies it and imprisonment need not be imposed (assumed, not ruled; NOTES.md, fork F-2024-3).
-- It is also 0 for the second and later misdemeanor, where imprisonment is required: the text states "not more than one year" and no minimum, so 0 there means that no minimum is stated.
-- A reader who holds that the text is merely silent about a minimum would answer NOTHING in all four cases.
-- The text words the value two ways ("such benefits are of a value of" and "the item ... is a benefit that has a value of"); the one value the person states stands for both (NOTES.md, fork F-2024-1).
GIVEN `the value of the benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the conviction is the second or a subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 2024 punishment`
`s 2024(b)(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the value of the benefits` LESS THAN 0 THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a value below zero is not a value of benefits
            NOTHING
        --                                                   grade,           fine max, term min, term max, prison required
        IF `the value of the benefits` AT LEAST 5000 THEN
            JUST (`s 2024 punishment` OF `s 2024 a felony`,       250000,   0,        20,       FALSE)
        IF `the value of the benefits` AT LEAST 100 AND (NOT `the conviction is the second or a subsequent conviction`) THEN
            JUST (`s 2024 punishment` OF `s 2024 a felony`,       10000,    0,        5,        FALSE)
        IF `the value of the benefits` AT LEAST 100 THEN
            JUST (`s 2024 punishment` OF `s 2024 a felony`,       10000,    0.5,      5,        TRUE)
        IF NOT `the conviction is the second or a subsequent conviction` THEN
            JUST (`s 2024 punishment` OF `s 2024 a misdemeanor`,  1000,     0,        1,        FALSE)
        OTHERWISE
            JUST (`s 2024 punishment` OF `s 2024 a misdemeanor`,  1000,     0,        1,        TRUE)

-- src:1888 | In addition to such penalties, any person convicted of a felony or misdemeanor violation under this subsection may be suspended by the court from participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program for an additional period of up to eighteen months consecutive to that period of suspension mandated by section 2015(b)(1) of this title.
@ref s 2024(b)(1) the court may suspend the person from the program for up to eighteen months more (src:1888)
-- In plain words: a person convicted of a felony or misdemeanor under this subsection may also be suspended by the court from the program for up to 18 more months, after the suspension that section 2015(b)(1) requires.
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of a felony or misdemeanor violation under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional suspension proposed, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2024(b)(1) the court may suspend the person for the additional period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has been convicted of a felony or misdemeanor violation under this subsection` AND `the additional suspension proposed, in months` AT MOST 18 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for an additional period of up to eighteen months consecutive to that period of suspension mandated by section 2015(b)(1) of this title"
            NOTHING

-- src:1888 | In addition to such penalties, any person convicted of a felony or misdemeanor violation under this subsection may be suspended by the court from participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program for an additional period of up to eighteen months consecutive to that period of suspension mandated by section 2015(b)(1) of this title.
@ref s 2024(b)(1) the longest additional suspension the court may order (src:1888)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of a felony or misdemeanor violation under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of ineligibility`
`s 2024(b)(1) the longest additional suspension` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has been convicted of a felony or misdemeanor violation under this subsection` THEN JUST (`for a number of months` 18)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person convicted of a felony or misdemeanor violation under this subsection"
            NOTHING

-- src:1889 | (2) In the case of any individual convicted of an offense under paragraph (1) of this subsection, the court may permit such individual to perform work approved by the court for the purpose of providing restitution for losses incurred by the United States and the State agency as a result of the offense for which such individual was convicted. If the court permits such individual to perform such work and such individual agrees thereto, the court shall withhold the imposition of the sentence on the condition that such individual perform the assigned work. Upon the successful completion of the assigned work the court may suspend such sentence.
@ref s 2024(b)(2) work approved by the court as restitution (src:1889)
-- In plain words: a person convicted of the offence may be allowed by the court to do court-approved work to make up the loss to the United States and the State agency. If the court allows it and the person agrees,
-- the court must hold back the sentence on condition the work is done; when it is done successfully the court may suspend the sentence.
GIVEN `the individual has been convicted of an offense under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2024(b)(2) the court may permit the individual to perform work approved by the court for restitution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the individual has been convicted of an offense under paragraph (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any individual convicted of an offense under paragraph (1) of this subsection"
            NOTHING

-- src:1889 | (2) In the case of any individual convicted of an offense under paragraph (1) of this subsection, the court may permit such individual to perform work approved by the court for the purpose of providing restitution for losses incurred by the United States and the State agency as a result of the offense for which such individual was convicted. If the court permits such individual to perform such work and such individual agrees thereto, the court shall withhold the imposition of the sentence on the condition that such individual perform the assigned work. Upon the successful completion of the assigned work the court may suspend such sentence.
@ref s 2024(b)(2) the court shall withhold the imposition of the sentence (src:1889)
GIVEN `the court permits the individual to perform the work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual agrees to perform the work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2024(b)(2) the court must withhold the imposition of the sentence on the condition that the work is performed` MEANS
