§§ `s 2024(c) presentation for payment or redemption of benefits that have been illegally received, transferred, or used`

-- src:1891 | Whoever presents, or causes to be presented, benefits for payment or redemption of the value of $100 or more, knowing the same to have been received, transferred, or used in any manner in violation of the provisions of this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter
@ref s 2024(c) whoever presents benefits for payment or redemption knowing they were received, transferred or used in violation (src:1891)
GIVEN `the person presented, or caused to be presented, benefits for payment or redemption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knew the benefits to have been received, transferred, or used in a manner in violation of this chapter or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2024(c) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person presented, or caused to be presented, benefits for payment or redemption` AND `the person knew the benefits to have been received, transferred, or used in a manner in violation of this chapter or the regulations` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "knowing the same to have been received, transferred, or used in any manner in violation of the provisions of this chapter or the regulations"
            NOTHING

-- src:1891 | of the value of $100 or more, knowing the same to have been received, transferred, or used in any manner in violation of the provisions of this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter, shall be guilty of a felony and, upon the first conviction thereof, shall be fined not more than $20,000 or imprisoned for not more than five years, or both, and, upon the second and any subsequent conviction thereof, shall be imprisoned for not less than one year nor more than five years and may also be fined not more than $20,000, or, if such benefits are of a value of less than $100, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor and, upon the first conviction thereof, shall be fined not more than $1,000 or imprisoned for not more than one year, or both, and, upon the second and any subsequent conviction thereof, shall be imprisoned for not more than one year and may also be fined not more than $1,000.
@ref s 2024(c) the punishment, by the value of the benefits and the number of convictions (src:1891)
-- In plain words: $100 or more is a felony: the first conviction, a fine up to $20,000 or up to 5 years, or both; the second and later, prison of 1 to 5 years and perhaps also a fine up to $20,000.
-- Under $100 is a misdemeanor: the first conviction, a fine up to $1,000 or up to 1 year, or both; the second and later, prison up to 1 year and perhaps also a fine up to $1,000.
GIVEN `the value of the benefits presented` IS A NUMBER
      `the conviction is the second or a subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 2024 punishment`
`s 2024(c) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the value of the benefits presented` LESS THAN 0 THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a value below zero is not a value of benefits
            NOTHING
        --                                                       grade,           fine max, term min, term max, prison required
        IF `the value of the benefits presented` AT LEAST 100 AND (NOT `the conviction is the second or a subsequent conviction`) THEN
            JUST (`s 2024 punishment` OF `s 2024 a felony`,       20000,    0,        5,        FALSE)
        IF `the value of the benefits presented` AT LEAST 100 THEN
            JUST (`s 2024 punishment` OF `s 2024 a felony`,       20000,    1,        5,        TRUE)
        IF NOT `the conviction is the second or a subsequent conviction` THEN
            JUST (`s 2024 punishment` OF `s 2024 a misdemeanor`,  1000,     0,        1,        FALSE)
        OTHERWISE
            JUST (`s 2024 punishment` OF `s 2024 a misdemeanor`,  1000,     0,        1,        TRUE)

