§§ `s 2024(e) forfeiture of property involved in illegal benefit transactions`

-- src:1895 | The Secretary may subject to forfeiture and denial of property rights any nonfood items, moneys, negotiable instruments, securities, or other things of value that are furnished by any person in exchange for benefits, or anything of value obtained by use of an access device, in any manner contrary to this chapter or the regulations issued under this chapter.
@ref s 2024(e) the Secretary may subject to forfeiture and denial of property rights things furnished in exchange for benefits (src:1895)
-- In plain words: the Secretary may take by forfeiture any nonfood items, money, negotiable instruments, securities or other things of value that a person furnished in exchange for benefits, or anything of value got by using an access device, in a way the chapter or its regulations forbid.
GIVEN `the property was furnished by a person in exchange for benefits, or was obtained by use of an access device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exchange or use was in a manner contrary to this chapter or the regulations issued under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2024(e) the Secretary may subject the property to forfeiture and denial of property rights` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the property was furnished by a person in exchange for benefits, or was obtained by use of an access device` AND `the exchange or use was in a manner contrary to this chapter or the regulations issued under this chapter` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "furnished by any person in exchange for benefits, or anything of value obtained by use of an access device, in any manner contrary to this chapter"
            NOTHING

-- src:1895 | Any forfeiture and disposal of property forfeited under this subsection shall be conducted in accordance with procedures contained in regulations issued by the Secretary.
@ref s 2024(e) forfeiture and disposal follow the procedures in the Secretary's regulations (src:1895)
GIVEN `the forfeiture and disposal was conducted in accordance with procedures contained in regulations issued by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2024(e) the forfeiture and disposal were conducted as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the forfeiture and disposal was conducted in accordance with procedures contained in regulations issued by the Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be conducted in accordance with procedures contained in regulations issued by the Secretary"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `s 2024(f) criminal forfeiture`

-- src:1897 | (1) In general
-- src:1898 | In imposing a sentence on a person convicted of an offense in violation of subsection (b) or (c), a court shall order, in addition to any other sentence imposed under this section, that the person forfeit to the United States all property described in paragraph (2).
@ref s 2024(f)(1) the court shall order forfeiture of the property described in paragraph (2) (src:1897-1898)
GIVEN `the person was convicted of an offense in violation of subsection (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2024(f)(1) the court must order the person to forfeit to the United States all property described in paragraph (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person was convicted of an offense in violation of subsection (b) or (c)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person convicted of an offense in violation of subsection (b) or (c)"
            NOTHING

-- src:1899 | (2) Property subject to forfeiture
-- src:1900 | All property, real and personal, used in a transaction or attempted transaction, to commit, or to facilitate the commission of, a violation (other than a misdemeanor) of subsection (b) or (c), or proceeds traceable to a violation of subsection (b) or (c), shall be subject to forfeiture to the United States under paragraph (1).
@ref s 2024(f)(2) property subject to forfeiture (src:1899-1900)
-- In plain words: all property, real and personal, used in or to commit or help commit a violation of (b) or (c) that is not a misdemeanor, and the proceeds traceable to a violation of (b) or (c).
GIVEN `the property was used in a transaction or attempted transaction, to commit, or to facilitate the commission of, a violation of subsection (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the violation was a misdemeanor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is proceeds traceable to a violation of subsection (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2024(f)(2) the property is subject to forfeiture to the United States` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the property is proceeds traceable to a violation of subsection (b) or (c)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the property was used in a transaction or attempted transaction, to commit, or to facilitate the commission of, a violation of subsection (b) or (c)` AND (NOT `the violation was a misdemeanor`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the property was used in a transaction or attempted transaction, to commit, or to facilitate the commission of, a violation of subsection (b) or (c)` AND `the violation was a misdemeanor` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a violation (other than a misdemeanor) of subsection (b) or (c)"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names property used in a violation and proceeds traceable to one, and does not say that no other property is subject to forfeiture
            NOTHING

-- src:1901 | (3) Interest of owner
