@ref s 2024(f)(3) the interest of an owner without knowledge or consent is not forfeited (src:1901-1902)
GIVEN `the owner established that the act or omission was committed or omitted without the knowledge or consent of the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2024(f)(3) the interest of the owner in the property may be forfeited as the result of the act or omission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the owner established that the act or omission was committed or omitted without the knowledge or consent of the owner` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No interest in property shall be forfeited under this subsection as the result of any act or omission established by the owner of the interest to have been committed or omitted without the knowledge or consent of the owner"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "established by the owner of the interest to have been committed or omitted without the knowledge or consent of the owner"
